'''Montjueu''' or '''Montjuich''' ({{Langx|ca|Montjuïc|4=Jewish Mountain}}) is a [[Regions of Balisca|region]] of the [[Hesperia|Hesperian community]] within the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. It was initially settled by {{W|Sephardic Jews}}, [[Mozbayana|Mozbayáns]] and [[W:Arab-Berber|Arab-Berber]]<nowiki/>s exiled from their homes around the Mesogean basin. The legacy of Tartessia has re-emerged in the 21st century out of a desire for preservation of Tartessian culture, the [[W:Judaeo-Spanish|Judaeo-Spanish language]] (Ladino), and their intimate historical ties to the [[W:Mediterranean World|Mediterranean world]].

'''Tartessianism''' ({{lang-bl|tartésianismo}}) is a primarily {{W|regionalism|regionalist}} political movement active in most of what is today considered within the Tartessian region that seeks to highlight the influences and contributions to the [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]] and it's [[Society of Balisca|society]] since the 16th century.

Historically speaking, the Jewish exiles played a significant role in the development of early Baliscan identity, and contemporary movements seek to promote the rediscovery of Judeo-Baliscan heritage, traditions, culture, and language. 

